    "message": "fix(php): count namespace blocks at the parser, not from entity scopes\n\nThe multi-namespace guard skipped a file when its entities carried more\nthan one distinct packageScope. Two shapes slip past that:\n\n  namespace A { use Vendor\\Thing; }   // declares nothing -> no scope\n  namespace B { class Thing {} ... }\n\n  namespace A { use Vendor\\Thing; }   // two blocks, one scope *string*\n  namespace A { class Thing {} ... }\n\nIn both, `use` from the first block was applied to the second, resolving\na name the second block declares itself and pointing it confidently at\nthe wrong file — the exact mis-resolution the guard exists to prevent.\n\nCount `namespace_definition` nodes instead, which is what the guard\nactually means. The count rides along on the walk that already collects\nthe unbraced spans: reading `namedChildren` a second time would pay the\nnode-wrapper materialization cost twice, and that term is what made the\noriginal per-definition scan expensive.\n\n`phpNamespaceBlocks` is spread in rather than assigned `undefined` so the\nkey is absent on non-PHP results — a present-but-undefined key still\nserializes and would have rewritten every checked-in parseFile snapshot.",
